On Friday 06 August 2004 19:58 Cyde Weys (cyde@umd.edu) wrote:

> Name: Dragoneater
> Reqs: Eat 20 dragon (not baby dragon) corpses.
> Rews: Gain a random dragon intrinsic.

Erm, if you eat 20 dragon corpses you're likely to have all the dragon
intrinsics already. At least those you can gain from eating: you can
never become magic resistant or acid resistant by eating dragon
corpses.

> Name: Fire Eater
> Reqs: Eat anything that is on fire, e.g. lit candle, lamp, etc.
> Rews: {Anyone got any ideas?}

Become fire resistant, of course.

> Name: Fortune Teller
> Reqs: Eat 5 fortune cookies.
> Rews: Get minor oracularities instead of random messages when eating
> fortune cookies.

Even cursed fortune cookies? (Blessed fortune cookies give minor
oracularities already, or rather, the Oracle gives true fortune-cookie
messages as minor oracularities)

> Name: Worm Rider
> Reqs: Kill 10 long worms.
> Rews: Gives a bonus to taming long worms and allows you to ride them
> (is that possible?).

No, worms can't be ridden because they can't be saddled.

> Name: Agnostic
> Reqs: Change alignment twice.
> Rews: {Anyone got any ideas?}

You can't change alignment twice, except by wearing a helm of opposite
alignment. Do you propose to change that as well?

